<li id="CR4">
<span class="label">4.</span><cite>Kross E, et al.  Self-talk as a regulatory mechanism: how you do it matters. Journal of personality and social psychology. 2014;106:304–324. doi: 10.1037/a0035173.</cite> [<a href="https://doi.org/10.1037/a0035173" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DOI</a>] [<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24467424/" class="usa-link">PubMed</a>] [<a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=Journal%20of%20personality%20and%20social%20psychology&amp;title=Self-talk%20as%20a%20regulatory%20mechanism:%20how%20you%20do%20it%20matters&amp;author=E%20Kross&amp;volume=106&amp;publication_year=2014&amp;pages=304-324&amp;pmid=24467424&amp;doi=10.1037/a0035173&amp;" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar</a>]</li>
<li id="CR5">
<span class="label">5.</span><cite>Grossmann I, Kross E. Exploring Solomon’s Paradox: Self-Distancing Eliminates the Self-Other Asymmetry in Wise Reasoning About Close Relationships in Younger and Older Adults. Psychological science. 2014;25:1571–1580. doi: 10.1177/0956797614535400.</cite> [<a href="https://doi.org/10.1177/0956797614535400" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DOI</a>] [<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24916084/" class="usa-link">PubMed</a>] [<a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=Psychological%20science&amp;title=Exploring%20Solomon%E2%80%99s%20Paradox:%20Self-Distancing%20Eliminates%20the%20Self-Other%20Asymmetry%20in%20Wise%20Reasoning%20About%20Close%20Relationships%20in%20Younger%20and%20Older%20Adults&amp;author=I%20Grossmann&amp;author=E%20Kross&amp;volume=25&amp;publication_year=2014&amp;pages=1571-1580&amp;pmid=24916084&amp;doi=10.1177/0956797614535400&amp;" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar</a>]</li>
<li id="CR6">
<span class="label">6.</span><cite>Kross, E., &amp; Ayduk, O. Self-Distancing: Theory, Research and Current Directions. <em>Advances in Experimental Social Psychology</em><strong>55</strong>, 81–136 (2017).</cite>
